COLUMNS
int ID
string Directory // the map's folder under world/maps: proven from the bytes (docs/world-viewer/00-audit.md 3.1)
locstring MapName_lang // the map's name as the client stores it: supported in every client; not always the exact label the game shows
locstring Text2_lang // string columns whose meaning is not established; Text2-Text5 sit in the same slots in every layout
locstring Text3_lang
locstring Text4_lang
locstring Text5_lang
float Point // a world (X, Y) point on the map LocationMapID names (Retail, Beta): supported
int MapType // the form of the map's WDT: 1 a tile grid with no global world model, 2 a world model only (named by FileDataID), 4 a world model only (named by path; Retail), 3 no WDT this client can read: holds for every readable WDT of the four audited clients
int InstanceType // the code Difficulty.db2 gives the map's difficulties: supported (codes 1, 2 and 5 exercised)
int Code9 // not established
int AreaTableID // an AreaTable row standing for the map: supported
int LoadingScreenID // a LoadingScreens.db2 row
int TimeOfDayOverride // -1, or a time of day the map keeps (Retail: -1 on 1081 of 1187 maps, 0 to 1350 on 106; every value fits a day in minutes, [0, 1440): proven from the bytes); the name is the public definitions' (the only column of this file named so, docs/world-viewer/10-light-sky-fog.md 3.3), the unit (minutes) inferred
int ParentMapID // when set, a map whose world space this map shares: supported (-1 is "not set", which does not mean "no parent")
int WorldCopyOfMapID // Retail, Classic Era, MoP Classic: when set, a map part of whose world this map copies: supported (-1: not set)
int BetaCode14 // Classic Beta: the WorldCopyOfMapID slot holds 2-bit codes there; their meaning is not established
int Code15 // not established (1 bit, 0 in every client)
float Float16 // not established
int EraMoPCode16 // not established (Classic Era and MoP Classic only)
int LocationMapID // when set, the map an instance is located on (its Point lies there): proven in Classic Beta, supported elsewhere; -1 is "not set", and Classic Era and Beta also store 0 with no point
int Code18 // not established
int Code19 // not established
int ZoneMapFileDataID // a 128x128 grid of AreaTable IDs for the map
int WdtFileDataID // the map's WDT (Retail, Classic Beta): proven (00-audit.md 3.1); Classic Era and MoP Classic have no such column
int BetaCode22 // not established (Classic Beta only)
int Code22 // not established (Retail)
int Code23 // not established (Retail)
int BetaCode23 // not established (Classic Beta; the slot of Retail's Code22, its meaning not shown to be the same)
int BetaCode24 // not established (Classic Beta; the slot of Retail's Code23, its meaning not shown to be the same)
int EraMoPCode21 // not established (Classic Era and MoP Classic; the slot of Retail's Code22, its meaning not shown to be the same)
int Flags // three words of flags: four bits of the first two are copies of WDT header (MPHD) bits (supported); bit 0x2 of the third is set on 49 of 59 Classic Era maps, 75 of 285 MoP Classic maps, 49 of 73 Classic Beta maps and no Retail or PTR map (proven from the bytes; its meaning not established); the rest are not established

COMMENT Written for WoW Model Viewer's world map catalogue from the clients' own bytes; no outside definition was used, but
COMMENT for one name: TimeOfDayOverride, the public definitions' name of the column (docs/world-viewer/10-light-sky-fog.md).
COMMENT Every column of each layout is listed in file order, so the positions are right for the layouts below; only
COMMENT the named columns the catalogue reads (database.xml, table Map) carry established meanings. A neutral name that
COMMENT two layouts share means the same slot in the column order, not an established equal meaning. The evidence, and
COMMENT how far it goes per client, is in docs/world-viewer/02-map-catalog.md. A layout not listed here is not read.

